---
// REVIEW: Layer 2 interpretation for COMPASS-31, drafted for Craig's review.
// Static, always visible, rendered at build time. FAQ answers come from
// compass-31.content.ts and are shown word for word (they also feed the
// page's FAQPage JSON-LD).
import { FAQ, SOURCES } from '../../tools/compass-31.content';
import '../../styles/interpretation.css';

const s = SOURCES;
---

<section class="interpretation" aria-labelledby="understanding-compass-31">
	<h2 id="understanding-compass-31">Understanding your COMPASS-31 score</h2>

	<h3 id="what-it-measures">What the score measures</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.measures.a}</p>
	<p>
		Orthostatic intolerance counts for up to 40 points, gastrointestinal 25, secretomotor 15, bladder 10, and vasomotor
		and pupillomotor 5 each. It was distilled at the Mayo Clinic from a longer questionnaire using the answers of 405
		healthy volunteers (<a href={s.sletten.href} rel="noopener">{s.sletten.label}</a>), then checked in 66 people being
		assessed for nerve damage (<a href={s.treister.href} rel="noopener">{s.treister.label}</a>).
	</p>
	<p>{FAQ.pots.a}</p>

	<h3 id="score-bands">Score bands</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.normal.a}</p>
	<p>Instead there are reference points from individual studies:</p>
	<table class="interp-table">
		<caption>COMPASS-31 scores reported in published studies</caption>
		<thead>
			<tr><th scope="col">Score</th><th scope="col">What the study found</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><th scope="row">10</th><td>Screening cut-off for small fibre neuropathy: caught 93% of cases, but also flagged most people without it</td><td><a href={s.treister.href} rel="noopener">Treister 2015</a></td></tr>
			<tr><th scope="row">20</th><td>Threshold for moderate to severe symptoms; 66% of 2,314 adults with long COVID scored above it</td><td><a href={s.larsen.href} rel="noopener">Larsen 2022</a></td></tr>
			<tr><th scope="row">30</th><td>Best cut-off for separating biopsy-confirmed small fibre neuropathy from none</td><td><a href={s.treister.href} rel="noopener">Treister 2015</a></td></tr>
			<tr><th scope="row">55.3</th><td>Average among 160 women with POTS in an online survey</td><td><a href={s.blitshteyn.href} rel="noopener">Blitshteyn 2024</a></td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>{FAQ.score30.a}</p>

	<h3 id="change">What a change in score means</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.change.a}</p>

	<h3 id="what-it-does-not-measure">What it does not measure</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.diagnosis.a}</p>
	<p>
		If your orthostatic score is high, the <a href="/tools/nasa-lean-test/">NASA lean test</a> records the readings a POTS
		assessment uses, and the <a href="/tools/malmo-pots-score/">Malmö POTS score</a> and
		<a href="/tools/vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score/">Vanderbilt score</a> focus on symptoms when upright. The
		<a href="/evidence/plain-language-guide-post-viral-autonomic-dysfunction/">plain-language guide to post-viral
		autonomic dysfunction</a> explains how these symptoms fit together.
	</p>

	<h3 id="taking-it-to-your-gp">Taking this to your GP or consultant</h3>
	<p>
		Bring your total, the date, the six domain scores and, if you have one, the trend (the history above can be copied as
		text). Most GPs will not know the COMPASS-31, so say what it is: a validated 31-question measure of autonomic symptoms
		from the Mayo Clinic. Autonomic, cardiology and neurology specialists are more likely to recognise it. Use it to
		support a request for assessment, such as a lying and standing heart rate and blood pressure check, not as evidence
		of a diagnosis. See the <a href="/evidence/30-bpm-threshold-pots/">30 bpm threshold explainer</a> and
		<a href="/nhs/preparing-for-gp-appointment/">preparing for a GP appointment</a>.
	</p>

	<div class="tool-foot">
		<slot name="disclaimer" />
		<details class="sources" id="sources">
			<summary>Sources and licence</summary>
			<slot name="citation" />
			<ul class="interp-sources">
				<li>Sletten DM, Suarez GA, Low PA, Mandrekar J, Singer W. COMPASS 31: a refined and abbreviated Composite Autonomic Symptom Score. <em>Mayo Clin Proc</em> 2012;87(12):1196–201. <a href={s.sletten.href} rel="noopener">Full text</a></li>
				<li>Okdahl T, et al. Supplementary material 3: COMPASS-31 items and scoring algorithm. <em>BMJ Open</em> 2021;11:e038677. <a href={s.okdahl.href} rel="noopener">Article</a></li>
				<li>Treister R, O'Neil K, Downs HM, Oaklander AL. Validation of the Composite Autonomic Symptom Scale 31 (COMPASS-31) in patients with and without small fiber polyneuropathy. <em>Eur J Neurol</em> 2015;22(7):1124–30. <a href={s.treister.href} rel="noopener">Article</a></li>
				<li>Larsen NW, et al. Characterization of autonomic symptom burden in long COVID: a global survey of 2,314 adults. <em>Front Neurol</em> 2022;13:1012668. <a href={s.larsen.href} rel="noopener">Article</a></li>
				<li>Blitshteyn S, et al. Sexual dysfunction in postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome (POTS): a cross-sectional, case-control study. <em>J Clin Med</em> 2024;13(8):2274. <a href={s.blitshteyn.href} rel="noopener">Article</a></li>
			</ul>
		</details>
	</div>
</section>
